  <p>More makes and years are coming. We add a table only when it’s documented well enough to cite. See our <a href="/classic-vin-decoder/methodology/">methodology and sources</a>.</p>

  <h2>How to read the confidence labels</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Documented:</strong> the character’s meaning comes straight from a factory or club reference for that exact year and model.</li>
    <li><strong>Likely:</strong> the code matches a documented table, but something about the car can’t be proven from the number alone. For example, a Ford year digit that repeats every decade.</li>
    <li><strong>Can’t confirm:</strong> the code isn’t in a table we can cite. We show the raw code and won’t guess.</li>
  </ul>

